# Nohn Virtual World Law Layer — Communication Protocol Standard V2.1
# One of the four law-layer modules: defines the minimal protocol for semantic exchange across engines.

## 1. Universal Translator
- Objective: force vendor-private commands to be laundered into Nohn standard semantics, stripping vendors of their covert interpretive authority over commands.
- Standard envelope: `NOHN_MSG_LOGIC: <intent_type> | <payload>`, where payload is JSON.
- Unknown commands: private commands that cannot be recognized are downgraded to `NOHN_GENERIC_LOGIC`, preventing logic penetration (neither dropped nor silently executed).

## 2. Standard Vocabulary
- `NOHN_STANDARD_MOVE`: movement class (vendor example: TX_PRIVATE_MOVE)
- `NOHN_STANDARD_ACTION`: action / attack class (vendor example: WY_PRIVATE_ATTACK)
- `NOHN_STANDARD_COMMUNICATE`: emote / communication class (vendor example: MHY_PRIVATE_EMOTE)
- `NOHN_STANDARD_TRADE`: trade class
- `NOHN_STANDARD_GOVERNANCE`: governance / referendum class
- Every vendor-private command must be mappable onto the table above; anything unmappable is handled as `NOHN_GENERIC_LOGIC`.

## 3. Compliance Determination (for auditors)
- A world must satisfy all three at once: (1) cross-world messages use the `NOHN_MSG_LOGIC` standard envelope; (2) unknown commands are downgraded rather than dropped; (3) private commands are mappable onto the standard vocabulary.
- Any failure → communication compliance audit FAILED, and the world is isolated from the Nohn ecosystem.
